<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Crazy Horse</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1840–<a href="/years/1877">1877</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Tasunke Witko</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Crazy Horse was an Oglala Lakota war leader who resisted American expansion onto the northern Plains. He fought in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-clouds-war">Red Cloud's War</a>, at the Rosebud and, alongside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sitting-bull">Sitting Bull</a>, in the defeat of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-armstrong-custer">George Armstrong Custer</a> at the Little Bighorn in June 1876. He surrendered at Fort Robinson in 1877 and was killed there by a soldier's bayonet while being arrested.</p></div>
